 have  forgiven him  i love him very much jones great aunt  maddie long is the sister of his victim  she and her sister were extremely close  what would you tell governor abbott if  he's watching this interview  i think the governor should spare him  because he have changed and he's a  different  person than he used to be according to  the non-profit death penalty information  center  in texas a death penalty case costs an  average of 2.3 million dollars  about three times the cost of  imprisoning someone in a single cell  at the highest security level for 40  years  overall support for the death penalty is  declining in the u.s  according to a 2019 poll from gallup  only 36 percent of americans  chose the death penalty when asked  whether the death penalty or  life without possibility of parole is  the better penalty for murder  when you look at a case like this one  really the only question is whether  people believe that the death penalty is  an appropriate kind of punishment  for this particular set of facts paul  cassell is a professor at the college of  law  at the university of utah you can make  two arguments in support of the death  penalty  one is the utilitarian argument that we  can deter  crime by imposing the most serious  punishment for  first-degree murder and the other is the  retributive argument that if we look  backward we want the punishment to fit  the crime  republican governor greg abbott has only  granted clemency  one other time to someone on death row i  understand too that  if i do get clemson i know that  instead of dying on the 19th i may die  years later  but it won't be in the free room it'll  be in prison  and i can accept that because there's  other avenues and prisons that i can  take  to better myself and to better others  along the way  more than 120 thousand people have  signed a change.org petition  asking texas governor greg abbott to  grant jones clemency  we reached out to the governor's office  but did not hear back  the texas board of pardon and paroles is  considering clemency  and once they make their decision which  could actually happen today  they'll pass that recommendation on to  governor abbott vlad  all right we'll be watching omar thank  you very much
 

